From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: in dark mode the controls are dark, whatever the frames' look

The Horizon and Glass looks (Style Frame 1 and 2) took their own colour
schemes (0743), which are light only, in either app mode: with dark mode
on, windows were dark and their combo boxes, scroll bars and buttons
light (regression walk 2026-10-05, Horizon + Dark). In dark mode the
controls now take the Dark scheme (Rounded Dark with the Rounded style);
the looks' frames stay theirs (0742). Light mode is unchanged.

Test: test/eraschemes-gate.sh, new check "Frame 1 in dark mode" (mutant
SG_MUTANT_ERA_LIGHT_IN_DARK).
---
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -662,7 +662,16 @@
     len = sizeof(frame);
     RegGetValueW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Style", L"Frame", RRF_RT_REG_DWORD, NULL, &frame, &len);
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_NOERASCHEMES
-    if (frame == 1 || frame == 2) MSSTYLES_OpenThemeFile(theme, frame == 1 ? L"Horizon" : L"Glass", size[0] ? size : NULL, &rounded);
+    /* in dark mode the controls are dark, whatever the frames' look: the
+     * era schemes are light only, and Horizon or Glass with dark mode left
+     * light combo boxes and scroll bars in dark windows (regression walk
+     * 2026-10-05) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ERA_LIGHT_IN_DARK
+    if ((frame == 1 || frame == 2) && !dark_mode)
+#else
+    if (frame == 1 || frame == 2)
+#endif
+        MSSTYLES_OpenThemeFile(theme, frame == 1 ? L"Horizon" : L"Glass", size[0] ? size : NULL, &rounded);
 #endif
     if (style && !rounded) MSSTYLES_OpenThemeFile(theme, dark_mode ? L"RoundedDark" : L"Rounded", size[0] ? size : NULL, &rounded);
     if (SUCCEEDED(MSSTYLES_OpenThemeFile(theme, NULL, size[0] ? size : NULL, &light)))
